<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hammurabi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1792–1750 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hammurabi was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> who reigned c. 1792–1750 BCE and built the Babylonian Empire across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. He defeated a coalition including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> in 1764 BCE and went on to conquer rival states. He is best known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi">Code of Hammurabi</a>, one of the most complete surviving legal codes of the ancient world, which influenced later traditions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hammurabi.jpg" alt="Hammurabi" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mbzt · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F0182_Louvre_Code_Hammourabi_Bas-relief_Sb8_rwk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
